{"nodes": [{"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "label": "Notebook: Run 2 - learning curve + boundary oversampling on laya_v1 (2 epochs)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Second run after run 1, six trainings in ~1h45. Answers (1) is more data worth generating (25/50/75/100 percent of the 57 training lectures) and (2) why the boundary question collapsed to always COMPLETE_SPAN. Changes vs run 1: 2 epochs (val loss lowest at epoch 2), boundary scored by balanced accuracy, a no-model word-overlap rule as the bar to beat, --boundary-oversample flag. Val and test unchanged so numbers compare directly. Hub repos ZenoAbderrahim/laya-wahy-lc-<run> for curve_100, bnd_x3, bnd_x6."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_curve_100", "label": "Run 2 curve_100 (all 57 lectures, 2,863 rows, soft_asis at 2 epochs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reference run of run 2. Later benchmark: AUC 0.945, accuracy 89.4 percent, not-a-quote recall 85.2 percent, real rejected 9.9 percent on the user's cards (reused as the verdict reference line in runs 4-6)."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x3", "label": "Run 2 bnd_x3 (cut-off boundary items repeated 3x)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cut-off boundary items are 42 percent of boundary items; repeating them 3x stops the model winning by always answering COMPLETE_SPAN. Notebook text notes (and run 4 later confirms) that more boundary items lowered verdict AUC: 0.945 -> 0.93 -> 0.918."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x6", "label": "Run 2 bnd_x6 (cut-off boundary items repeated 6x)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cut-off items are 59 percent of boundary items after 6x repetition; asks whether more oversampling is better or makes the model too eager to flag cut-offs."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_curve_25_50_75", "label": "Run 2 curve_25 / curve_50 / curve_75 (nested stratified lecture subsets)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whole lectures (a lecture's findings are near-copies), nested so each step only adds data, stratified separately for the 9 review lessons (with the user's labels) and the 48 batch lectures; SEED 20261026. Weights deleted after evaluation (~1.2 GB each); only curve_100, bnd_x3, bnd_x6 weights kept."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_learning_curve_question", "label": "Learning-curve experiment: is generating more data worth it?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the 75 -> 100 percent segment still rises by more than the noise (~1-2 points, one seed per point) more data helps; if flat, effort should go to hard cases, errors and the boundary instead."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_boundary_oversample", "label": "--boundary-oversample (repeat cut-off boundary items in training)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cause of the collapse: 81 percent of training boundary labels are COMPLETE_SPAN (Sonnet marks 84-87 percent complete), so 'always complete' is cheapest and scored 86 percent accuracy on val, hiding the problem. Fix in train_ddp.py plus balanced accuracy (always-complete = 0.25). On the user's own cards the boundary is judged stricter (45 percent complete) so Sonnet-trained models under-flag."}], "edges": [{"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_wahy_finetuning_finished", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_curve_100", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x3", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x6", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_curve_25_50_75", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_curve_25_50_75", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_learning_curve_question", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x3", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_boundary_oversample", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_bnd_x6", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_boundary_oversample", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__laya-learning-curve-kaggle-finished.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__laya_learning_curve_kaggle_finished_boundary_oversample", "